WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.049
there's a chapter in my book called
don't ever don't let your children do

00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:08.160
anything that makes you dislike them and
I'm pretty happy about this chapter

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.480
although I suspect it'll be rather
controversial and you know that it's

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.590
predicated first on the observation that
many people hurt their children

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.859
physically and psychologically
you know because everyone gets

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:23.550
sentimental about the relationship
between parents and children but that's

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.930
especially in relationship to themselves
because they think well you know of

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.170
course I'm going to be a good parent
it's like it's not so bloody obvious

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:36.120
that you're gonna be a good parent you
know and so and then what I see

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.170
happening with people who don't know how
to discipline their children is that the

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.090
children run roughshod over them in
their let's call them hierarchical

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.840
disputes because children push for
position in hierarchy and they do that

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.500
behaviorally to sort of feel out the
contours of the social structure so you

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.480
know your kid locked perfectly fine at
home let's say at the dinner table but

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.910
then you take them to a stranger's
dinner table and all of a sudden they

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:04.290
act out and you think what's up with you
you little monster and what's up is that

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.680
they're trying to figure out what the
power structure is in the new they don't

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.860
know this of course but they're acting
this out they're trying to figure out if

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.400
the same rules apply in this new
situation as apply in the old situation

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.259
and they can't ask that and they don't
even know that they are rules exactly

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:23.189
they're regularities that they've
learned and so they'll test and test and

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:26.909
then you have to show them that yeah
it's the same here it's the same in this

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:32.070
situation but lots of parents are very
uneasy with disciplining their children

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.880
partly because they're they believe that
if you give a child infinite freedom

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.240
that's best for them and that
constraints are inappropriate which is

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.619
really just well I don't know what to
say about that except it's so untrue

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:47.759
that that it's very difficult to think
of anything that's more untrue than that

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:52.380
but also the thing is is if you let your
children take advantage of you if you

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.960
have an ounce of spine and an ounce of
aggression which you do especially if

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:02.820
you don't admit it then you will take
revenge on your children you know so if

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.600
they have a temper tantrum in a grocery
store and embarrass you which a child

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.110
whose County can do quite effectively
you know because you wouldn't let them

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:13.240
have that pack of crayons or a chocolate
bar

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:17.230
and then you know you you tell yourself
it's okay and that you still you know

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:20.800
that that really didn't make you that
angry and it's okay but you're fuming

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.790
inside and then you go home and half an
hour later maybe the child is doing some

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.690
interesting little bit of work maybe
artwork or something or does something

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:33.100
good and comes up for a reward it's like
the probability that you're gonna reward

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:37.180
that child properly under those
circumstances zero you're gonna take the

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.410
opportunity to take your revenge and if
you don't know that then you're not much

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:48.070
of a parent and so part of the trick
with kids is that if your child is doing

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.950
something that makes you dislike them
that you have to figure out how to stop

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:54.310
them from doing that and teach them how
to do it properly and you have to talk

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:57.760
to your wife to make sure that you're
not being too much of a monster you know

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:03.970
and the same with her but that that
discipline is partly what enables you to

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:08.410
continue to like your child well you
love them and even more than that you

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:12.790
know parents talk about fostering
self-esteem and fostering creativity and

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.170
all of that and their kids and I think
that's misbegotten

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:21.160
it's shallow for a variety of reasons
first it's not that easy to foster

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.850
creativity because it's rare and
self-esteem is a very badly defined

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.230
concept and mostly it's been used for
harm not good what your job is as a

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:35.920
parent is to help your child learn from
between two years old and say four years

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:41.380
old how to act in the world so that when
people encounter them people smile and

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:45.910
are happy they're around because then
you know I've seen kids who behave badly

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:51.160
and everywhere they go people wear false
smiles and everywhere they go people are

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.820
relieved when they leave and that means
you think about that world from the

00:03:54.820 --> 00:04:00.220
child's perspective everyone's lying and
all everyone hates them that's their

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:07.270
world and then if you have your child
you know capable of adhering to minimal

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:11.410
social requirements like maybe being
able to sit at the tables in a civilized

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:16.090
manner for an hour and being grateful
for being fed let's say and knowing how

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:20.530
to share and knowing how to pay
attention to adults and and not having

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:28.660
that you know that kind of
terrible cynicism and and arrogance that

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.040
can develop even in a four-year-old
child who's always had its way then then

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.700
they'll interact with adults in a manner
that bring out the best and the adults

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.420
and every year they go everyone smiles
at them and Pat's them on the head maybe

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.260
even tells them useful and interesting
things and so the whole world opens up

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.730
for them and that's all a consequence of
you having enough courage to admit to

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:53.650
yourself that your child can do things
that you don't like and that you will

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.100
take it out on them if you don't
straighten it out and people don't like

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.460
that idea because they think well I'd
never do anything you know I love my

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.730
child I'd never do anything to hurt them
it's like yeah Oh God

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:09.040
right you know you're so you're so
asleep if you think that that that

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:14.170
there's almost no hope for you you have
to think I'm way bigger than this child

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:19.840
and I'm way meaner and I'm wait Rekia
and I'm Way more unpredictable and so I

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.430
better be very careful in my
relationships with this child so that

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.540
the worst of me doesn't come out and
then that gives you enough intelligence

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:34.300
to make a disciplinary framework that's
minimal and enforce it properly and

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.510
carefully

